.TH YLR-AUTO 1 "November 2026" "YLR-Auto 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ylr-auto \- rip discs with MakeMKV and file them into Jellyfin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ylr-auto
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.br
.B ylr-auto
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ylr-auto
rips discs from each optical drive through makemkvcon, and watches rips started
in MakeMKV's own window. It files finished rips into Jellyfin libraries using
names and posters from TMDb. Films that match exactly one TMDb entry by name and
runtime, or the runtime of a film you picked before ripping, can be filed
automatically, and anything uncertain waits for you. MakeMKV is a separate
program and is not included.
.PP
Closing the window keeps the program and its rips running from the tray. Use the
tray menu to quit, which warns first and stops any rips.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start in the tray with no window. Login startup uses this.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMDB_API_KEY
TMDb API key or read access token. Overrides the saved key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/littlerippa\-autosort/config.json
Settings, including the TMDb key. Readable by the owner only.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/littlerippa\-autosort/autosort.log
Record of rips and file moves.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/littlerippa\-autosort/posters
Cached TMDb posters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR makemkvcon (1)
.PP
https://github.com/cpntodd/YLR\-Auto
